bg3le crash handler: name the Ext.UI call that was running (function, key, object, class)

On top of 0001-0014. bg3le-20261106-011048 (l_get on a free-list word) left the C function in the stack scan and the
object's address in a register, but not the property name or the class, and systemd-coredump stored no core (no space on
/), so neither could be recovered afterwards.

- serialized() keeps a note on its stack for each call: the C function and its string argument (arg 2, the property name
  for UiGet/UiSet). object_arg adds the first object, and the box's Counted and class name, recorded when the box is made.
- The crash handler prints the notes of the crashing thread first, innermost first, then each object's first word and the
  word at +8 (the count, on a counted object). Crashes with no call on the thread say so. Everything that can be gone is
  read through safe_read, so this can't fault inside the handler before the registers are logged.

Costs a 63-byte copy per Ext.UI call and one pointer per box. Test: tools/test_bg3le_ui_refs.py.
Against bg3le 3728a68 (v0.3.6) with 0001-0014. Applied by tools/build_bg3le.sh.
